Hello!

We’ve updated the game with some fixes and specific improvements:


 Fixed the bugs that prevented Night 2 from starting;
 Rebalanced the speed of Spawnlings and the reaction time of Unsmillers;
 Party Balloon now starts with two balloons and can evolve up to 6;
 To unlock Night 2, it’s no longer necessary to survive Night 1. You just need to survive until 6 AM. What happens after 6 AM becomes an optional challenge to unlock the remaining content ;)


If you're still encountering bugs related to game loading, feel free to contact us at support@n3bula.com.br so we can help recover your save file if possible.

Thanks for the feedback, and see you next time!

First, we would like to thank everyone who played and explored the mysteries and dangers of Millennium Park over this first year. Now, we proudly present Night 2, with significant improvements and lots of new features!


 New weapon upgrade system. Now, weapons will receive new upgrades and specific attributes at each level, with better scalability and variation in the potential of your arsenal;

 Fixes for critical bugs that caused the game to crash when defeated or when completing a night;

 Improvements to enemy AI, with better detection of the environment and reactions to the player;

 Improvements to item selection on the Level Up! screen, with better distribution of collectible items, prioritizing only those that will actually be useful to the player;

 Significant visual improvements, with new adjustment settings;

 Added Spanish to the list of languages;

 8 new weapons, 9 new equippable items, and 3 collectible items (plus a chaotic secret);


We will continue to pay attention to your feedback. Thank you for your support, and we’ll see you soon!

Hey guys!
Today we are releasing our version 1.0.5, with bug fixes and some improvements:

- Fixed the annoying camera bug caused by combining the Measuring Tape item with some specific weapons, such as the Party Balloon and Candle;
- Added new screen resolution option in settings;
- Adjusts to some particle systems that were damaging performance;
- Added new ability for Boomerang: now it collects XP scattered around the scenario and brings it to you!
- Lantern no longer shines light on objects in the scene, avoiding lighting errors;
- Consumable items will now only appear on the Level Up screen from level 5 onwards;
- XP Orbs now have different colors according to how many points they are worth;
- More abundant consumable items throughout the scenario;
- Minor adjustments and rebalancing

Stay tuned for big news soon!

